      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"Statistical Analysis & Predictive Modeling\"\n",
        "page-layout: full\n",
        "title-block-banner: false\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "<style>\n",
        "/* Completely hide Quarto's default automatic title block */\n",
        "#title-block-header {\n",
        "  display: none !important;\n",
        "}\n",
        "</style>\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column-screen style=\"background-color: #f8f9fa; padding: 50px 0 40px 0; margin-bottom: 20px; border-bottom: 1px solid #e0e0e0;\"}\n",
        "::: {.container style=\"max-width: 1100px; padding-left: 15px; padding-right: 15px;\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "<h1 style=\"font-size: 2.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: #1a1a1a; margin-bottom: 25px; margin-top: 0;\">Statistical Analysis & Predictive Modeling</h1>\n",
        "\n",
        "# The Collapse of the Eastern Bering Sea Snow Crab\n",
        "### How Spatial Modeling & Historical Back-Casting Explained an Ecological Catastrophe\n",
        "***\n",
        "###  Project Navigation\n",
        "* <a href=\"#README\" target=\"_self\" style=\"font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline;\">README</a> — <em>Jump directly to the full research breakdown below.</em>\n",
        "* **[CODE](crab_project.html)** - *Review the documented R Markdown processing scripts, models, and diagnostic plots.*\n",
        "* **[DATA](data/mfsnowcrab.csv)** — *Historical NOAA bottom-trawl survey records used in this study. Originally sourced from [Kaggle](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/mattop/snowcrab)*\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.container style=\"max-width: 1100px; padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 60px;\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "## At a Glance\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.columns style=\"display: flex; gap: 40px; margin-bottom: 40px;\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "### Core Methodologies\n",
        "* Linear & Quadratic Discriminant Analysis (LDA/QDA)\n",
        "* 2D-Kernel Density Estimation (KDE)\n",
        "* Polynomial OLS Regression\n",
        "* Feature Aggregation & Pipeline Development\n",
        "* Historical Data Reconstruction (Back-Casting/Reverse Forecasting)\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "### Business Impact & Domain Value\n",
        "* **Overcoming Critical Data Blackouts:** I mitigated multi-year data gaps caused by halted survey seasons, engineering a predictive model to simulate missing operational records and ensure long-term environmental planning continuity.\n",
        "\n",
        "* **Translating Complex Phenomena into Metrics:** I synthesized abstract mathematical concepts (like ecological \"climate traps\") into clear, strategic narratives tailored for non-technical stakeholders and executive decision-makers.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "***\n",
        "\n",
        "## Key Challenge: Non-Linear Skew & Spatial Decoupling\n",
        "\n",
        "* **The Technical Hurdle:** Initial predictive modeling struggled heavily with the right-skewed nature of fisheries catch data, yielding an $R^2$ of just **0.076** due to extreme data volatility and high-leverage catching anomalies. While a log-transformation was necessary, early base-R data aggregation pipelines inadvertently decoupled the spatial alignment of the dataset, causing the model to completely lose the signal of environmental predictors ($R^2 = \\textbf{0.015}$).\n",
        "\n",
        "* **The Solution:** I migrated the data pipeline to a unified `tidyverse` aggregation framework that precisely synchronized spatial and environmental metrics using individual haul signatures. Refitting the log-transformed response with a quadratic term for ocean depth unlocked the true dynamics of the ecosystem, expanding the model's explanatory power to **39.6%**. This architectural fix mathematically isolated both an explicit parabolic depth preference boundary and an acute negative population response to rising bottom temperatures.\n",
        "\n",
        "***\n",
        "## <span id=\"README\"></span>README\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "### 🌊 Executive Summary\n",
        "In 2021, NOAA Fisheries resumed data collection after global pandemic restrictions halted field surveys for two years. They discovered that during that data blackout, over **10 *billion* snow crabs** had vanished from the Eastern Bering Sea, effectively wiping out a historically stable population and crippling a lucrative \\$150M annual fishery, with no initial explanation. \n",
        "\n",
        "This project uses multivariate regression, discriminant analysis, and 2D kernel density estimation on historical NOAA bottom-trawl survey data (1975–2018) to \"back-cast\" the population’s likely location during the unmonitored 2019 season, a summer in which the predicted area experienced a record breaking marine heatwave. \n",
        "\n",
        "**The Core Finding:** The analysis reveals a mathematical **\"Climate Trap.\"** Decadal trends show the population steadily migrating northwest toward a structural dead-end. When the heatwave struck, the crabs were geographically bottlenecked in the shallow waters of Bristol Bay—bound by a strict, parabolic depth requirement and land barriers, leaving them with zero escape routes to cooler, deeper water.\n",
        "\n",
        "***\n",
        "\n",
        "### Core Research Questions & Key Insights\n",
        "\n",
        "#### 1. What environmental factors dictate catch success?\n",
        "* **Method:** Multivariate Linear Regression utilizing log-transformed Catch Per Unit Effort (CPUE) and quadratic features for bathymetric depth.\n",
        "\n",
        "* **Insight:** Population density is tightly bound to a non-linear \"Goldilocks Zone\" for depth. Both bottom depth and the quadratic term are ultra-significant. Rising bottom temperatures show an acute, crushing negative impact on density, **proving that cold-acclimated crabs actively flee warming waters**.\n",
        "\n",
        "#### 2. Do environmental niches diverge by sex?\n",
        "* **Method:** Linear & Quadratic Discriminant Analysis (LDA/QDA).\n",
        "\n",
        "* **Insight:** Classifiers yielded high cross-validated test error rates (~39.6% for QDA), revealing that males and females share an inseparable fundamental environmental niche. However, secondary spatial mapping uncovered behavioral segregation: **females cluster tightly along deep northwestern shelf** margins for egg preservation, whereas **males disperse widely southeast** to mitigate territorial aggression.\n",
        "\n",
        "#### 3. Can we track historical migration to locate the population during the data gap?\n",
        "* **Method:** 2D Kernel Density Estimation paired with joint linear vector modeling over time.\n",
        "\n",
        "* **Insight:** The Year variable alone explains **50.6%** of longitudinal variance and **44.4%** of latitudinal variance. **The population has followed a remarkably rigid, statistically ironclad trajectory northwest for decades**. \n",
        "\n",
        "***\n",
        "\n",
        "## 🛠️ Data Engineering & Pipeline Refactoring\n",
        "\n",
        "### The Data Alignment Challenge\n",
        "The raw NOAA dataset spans $n = 17,927$ individual specimen observations. Early modeling attempts in base R yielded a broken model with an $R^2$ of just **1.5%**, indicating that the environment had no statistical relationship with crab location. \n",
        "\n",
        "**The Bug:** Fragmented base-R `aggregate()` and `cbind()` scripts decoupled row synchronization across features. The model was inadvertently mapping the catch numbers of Haul A to the ocean depths of Haul B.\n",
        "\n",
        "**The Fix:** Migrating to a unified, declarative tidyverse pipeline forced all geospatial, biological, and thermal features to collapse simultaneously by their unique haul signatures:\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "```{qmd}\n",
        "# Synchronized Multi-Feature Aggregation Pipeline\n",
        "haul_df <- snowcrab_raw %>%\n",
        "  group_by(year, haul) %>%\n",
        "  summarize(\n",
        "    CPUE         = sum(cpue, na.rm = TRUE),\n",
        "    lat          = mean(latitude, na.rm = TRUE),\n",
        "    long         = mean(longitude, na.rm = TRUE),\n",
        "    bottom_depth = mean(bottom_depth, na.rm = TRUE),\n",
        "    surface_temp = mean(surface_temperature, na.rm = TRUE),\n",
        "    bottom_temp  = mean(bottom_temperature, na.rm = TRUE),\n",
        "    .groups = \"drop\"\n",
        "  ) %>%\n",
        "  mutate(CPUE_log = log(CPUE + 1)) # Guarding against log(0) calculation errors\n",
        "\n",
        "Upon executing this fix, the true ecological signals instantly locked into place, expanding the model's explanatory power from 1.5% to 39.6% (F=773.7,p<2.2×10−16).\n",
        "```"
      ],
